---
description: Which tests to run after a change, and how to keep builds fast
alwaysApply: true
---

# Run the tests the change can affect, not everything

Pick the smallest set that covers what changed; widen only when the change crosses modules.

| Changed | Run |
|---|---|
| `syncplay-protocol` | `gradlew :syncplay-protocol:test` (+ `scripts/sync-check.ps1` on a mobile device + TV only if sync timing changed) |
| `media-source` | `gradlew :media-source:test` |
| `shared` logic (controllers, settings, local library) | `gradlew :shared:desktopTest :app:testDebugUnitTest`, then the instrumented classes that use it |
| `shared/.../ui/mobile` | `android-safety-net.ps1 -SkipJvm -Tests <affected classes>` on phone + tablet, e.g. `MobileUiTest,MobileScreenshotTest` |
| TV UI (`app/.../ui/tv`, `ui/screens`) | `android-safety-net.ps1 -SkipJvm -Tests TvNavigationTest,TvScreenshotTest` |
| Player (`player-mpv`, `MobilePlayer.kt`) | `-Tests LocalPlaybackTest,MobileScreenshotTest#playerAndSheets` |
| One test file | just that class (or `Class#method`) |
| `player-mpv-desktop`, `desktop` | `gradlew :player-mpv-desktop:test :desktop:test` - no Android run |
| Scripts, docs, CI yaml, README | no emulator run; dry-run or lint what changed |

- Code moves between modules, dependency/Gradle/Compose version changes, theme or shared component changes:
  full `scripts/android-safety-net.ps1` (all devices + sync check) - pixel identity is the point there.
- Always run the full safety net once before a release/version bump.
- Follow test progress (phase log + `adb logcat -d -s TestRunner:I` per device) instead of blind waiting.

# Keep builds fast

- Don't run `gradlew --stop` or kill the Kotlin daemon between builds; warm daemons make an edit-build ~8 s
  instead of ~40 s. The safety-net script only stops them when it has to boot an emulator or the host has
  less than 6 GB free (paged-out emulators stall and ANR).

# Keep test runs fast and reliable

- The full net runs all devices in parallel, the JVM tests alongside when the host has 6 GB free, and the
  sync check on whichever of phone and tablet finishes first. It ends with each device's slowest tests.
- Leave the emulators running between runs. The script restarts one when it has been up for over 2 hours
  or its graphics allocator, System UI or launcher is spinning (worn emulators ran suites 2.5-4x slower),
  booting from the `yarmiplaytv_clean` snapshot in ~20-45 s; the first cold boot settles and saves it.
- Only one safety-net run uses the emulators at a time (a system-wide lock); a second run from another
  working copy waits instead of breaking both.
- A failure where logcat shows a long "Davey!" / "Skipped N frames" or "Application ANR likely" around
  the player's surface is the emulator GPU stalling mpv, not the test: rerun just that class.
- Use debug-variant tasks (`testDebugUnitTest`, `assembleDebug`), never bare `test`/`build` locally:
  those also compile release variants and run the desktop libmpv tests.
- Configuration cache is on: in build scripts, don't capture script-level vals/functions in task actions
  (copy them into a local `val` first).
